        <a
          href="https://nutakupublishing.helpshift.com/hc/en/87-zone-nova/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">nutakupublishing.helpshift.com</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Servers</h3>
    <p>
      There are currently 3 servers (as of Nov. 2026; you cannot use an account from one server
      for the other):
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>EroLabs (Web, mobile, PC)</li>
      <li>Nutaku (1 month behind in content. Web, mobile, PC)</li>
      <li>Steam (1 year behind in content, PC only)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="battles">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4030-cute.png"
        alt="Hiyori chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Battles Screen</h2>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Idle Rewards</h3>
    <p>
      Get aether points and bonding items for free. Maximum time limit: 24h. You can collect at
      any time you want. The rarity and size of the rewards depend on your story mode
      progression.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the free daily "Quick" rewards button for an additional 120 minutes of idle rewards.
      Usually, it is not worth it to invest Luminite for more!
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Arena</h3>
    <p>
      PvP area. Fights are done automatically. You can only set up the team, ultimate order and
      select the opponent (5 tries each day). For more details see the Pinnacle Arena section
      below.
    </p>
    <p>
      You earn "Arena Coins" that you can use to buy items in the "Arena Shop". Make sure to
      worship the current champion for a free 50 Luminites reward.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Raid</h3>
    <p>
      This has 4 categories: Raid, Annihilation Battle (AB), Temporal Rift, Trial.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Raid: Invest stamina to gain various resources. Use as needed to progress your
        characters. Also, this is the place when some missions ask you to do "resource raid",
        "veteran raid" or "rune raid". Tip: you can increase the challenge attempts to do several
        of them in one go. Saves lots of time.
      </li>
      <li>
        AB: Do as much damage as possible to a PvE boss within a time limit. 20x reward chests is
        the maximum (10M damage?). Then you can use the daily "sweep" to immediately claim the
        20x chests three times without battle. Use the coins to buy resources in the shop.
      </li>
      <li>Temporal Rift: Fight enemies with increasing difficulty for rewards.</li>
      <li>
        Rift Invasion (15 stages, stage 10+ requires 2 full teams instead of 1 team) is
        permanently available. Rift Surges (10 stages each, 2 full teams required) have a 2 week
        time limit (see the wiki for more details). Rift Laws apply that give active effects
        during battle. Click on the "Details" button to learn about the Rift Laws. Build your
        team accordingly!
      </li>
      <li>
        Trial: Fight enemies with increasing difficulty for rewards.
        <ul>
          <li>
            Adversity Trial: Permanently available. Trial of Freedom has no character
            restrictions. The other 4 trials have a limited 3 daily attempts and character
            restrictions. Note that these trials are also needed to complete some missions, so do
            them when you can!
          </li>
          <li>
            Trial of Bravery: 2 week limited event with character restrictions. The enemies are
            very tanky and there are active special effects. Click on "View Details" inside the
            Trial of Bravery window to see them. Build your team accordingly! More details on the
            wiki (note: Nutaku is 2 weeks behind EroLabs).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Story Mode Battle</h3>
    <p>
      Main source for account XP. Provides additional rewards. Increases rarity and size of
      "Idle Rewards". As of Nov. 2026, the maximum story mode chapter is Ch. 68-9.
    </p>
    <p>
      Enemy: Shows the enemy lineup, recommended damage types for your team and rewards for the
      next story mode battle.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Team</h3>
    <p>
      Shows the currently active team. A team consists of 4 characters and max 1 instance of a
      specific character. You can set up to 8 teams.
    </p>
    <p>
      The order of characters is important and can be changed. The first character is controlled
      by the player (keyboard: use WASD for movement, mouse for ultimates, Enter in the num lock
      area for activating the last ultimate). Enemies focus their damage on the first character.
      If she dies, then on the second character and so on.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you click on the left "combo" button, then it shows which combos are active in this
      team. Most of the time, you want to create a team where all 4 combos are active! However,
      in some situations, it is not possible for certain characters that are still worth using
      because they are very strong (e.g. Medusa).
    </p>
    <p>
      If you click on the "1-2-3" button at the bottom right, you can set up a character skill
      auto-queue for ultimates. However, this only works if "Auto" mode has been activated.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You can set multiple ultimates for round 1: just click into the area and select the
        character ultimates that you want to use. If only one round is set, skills will activate
        in queue order once enough energy is accumulated.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can set up multiple rounds the same way (maximum 20 rounds). If multiple rounds are
        set, skills will execute from lowest to highest round.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you click on "Auto Queue", then all rounds and ultimates are consolidated into fewer
        rounds (preserving the order).
      </li>
      <li>
        If you click on "Clear All", then all rounds are deleted. This cannot be undone. You must
        set up the ultimates again.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Stamina: Resource for raids. More details in the glossary.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="arena">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4017-cute.png"
        alt="Athena chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Pinnacle Arena</h2>
    <p>
      Pinnacle Arena is a stage to showcase your strength, where you can spar with other players.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sparring earns Arena Coins, which can be spent in the Arena Shop on growth items and
      bonding items characters love. Battles are fully automatic, with players setting formations
      and ULT queues beforehand.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Seasons</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Each season lasts 28 days, divided into 3 phases: Ranked Match, Pinnacle Tournament, and Worship.</li>
      <li>
        Each season includes 4 Ranked Matches and 1 Pinnacle Tournament. After crowning a
        Pinnacle champion, the season enters the Worship phase until the next champion emerges.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Ranked Match</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Ranked Matches span 27 days, with 4 matches per season. The first begins Monday at 04:00
        after a new season starts. Players have 5 daily Challenge Attempts, with extra attempts
        purchasable using Luminite Crystals. Attempts refresh daily at 04:00.
      </li>
      <li>
        Players start with 1000 points as Candidates. Each challenge consumes an attempt, earning
        varying Arena Coins based on victory or defeat.
      </li>
      <li>
        Winning against players adds points. Losing at Noble Platinum tier or above deducts
        points; otherwise, no deduction.
      </li>
      <li>Every 5 consecutive wins without refreshing the opponent list grants an extra challenge attempt.</li>
      <li>If points are tied at settlement, the player who reached the rank earlier takes precedence.</li>
      <li>
        Each Ranked Match ends at midnight Sunday, followed by reward settlement. Points remain
        static, and no sparring is allowed during this time.
      </li>
      <li>The top 32 players in the final Ranked Match's leaderboard qualify for the Pinnacle Tournament.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Pinnacle Tournament</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The top 32 from the final Ranked Match qualify.</li>
      <li>
        The brackets are predetermined: Rank 1 goes to bracket A, Rank 2 to bracket B, Rank 3 to
        bracket C, Rank 4 to bracket D, and Rank 5 restarts and goes back to bracket A. So it is
        important to choose which rank you want to be at by the end of the season.
      </li>
      <li>
        32 players are split into 4 groups of 8, battling in pairs. Each group produces 1 player
        for the Top 4 Slots, who advance to the Championship group for Semifinals and Finals to
        determine the champion and runner-up.
      </li>
      <li>
        On tournament day, from 04:00 to 15:15, participants can set their deployed teams. After
        15:15, the set teams are used for all duels until the tournament ends.
      </li>
      <li>Non-qualified players can bet on each Pinnacle match, earning returns for successful bets.</li>
      <li>Rewards for winning: profile card background, profile frame, up to 1600 Luminites.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Hall of Fame</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You can check the player teams and fully replay all battles of all tournament seasons
        that have ever happened.
      </li>
      <li>Click at the top right to select a season.</li>
      <li>Click on "Peak Review" for the details.</li>
      <li>
        Replaying a battle also provides a "statistics" button. It shows statistics for both
        players (e.g. damage dealt, damage taken, recovery amount).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Betting Record</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When the tournament starts, you can set bets on each match. More specifically: after the
        formation timer has ended (click on "Tournament", then the timer in the center above
        "Rewards". It is NOT the "Remaining" timer before clicking on "Tournament").
      </li>
      <li>
        The betting window is quite tight (45 minutes). You need to be there and bet before a
        match round starts (once every 1 hour).
      </li>
      <li>
        Investment is Arena Coins (500 to 1500 for each match; winning doubles the amount). So
        even if you lose, it is not that big as you have many Arena Coins, usually.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can see the total bettors count for a match near the name of the player. Maybe this
        is a good indicator on which team to bet on.
      </li>
      <li>
        After the matches are done, there is a 15 minutes cooldown until the next bets can be
        placed. After that, the new 45 minutes betting window begins.
      </li>
      <li>
        The betting record is updated at the end of the tournament. The Arena Coin winnings are
        given through the mail system.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="glossary">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4029-cute.png"
