  <section class="zguide-section" id="market">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4005-cute.png"
        alt="Cleopatra chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Market and Battle Pass (P2W)</h2>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Market</h3>
    <p>
      From the start page, the golden market icon is on the left side. It has P2W offers only!
      This guide offers P2W recommendations in terms of best value (in Luminites) per price.
    </p>
    <p>The market consists of 4 categories: Recommended, Monthly Pass, Featured, Recharge.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Recommended: These offers are better than the "recharge" ones, usually.</li>
      <li>
        Monthly Pass: Probably the best value per price. 3000 Luminites over the course of 30
        days for about 5.
      </li>
      <li>
        Featured: It has some specific offers. Usually, the offers are better than the "recharge"
        ones. Some have bigger value than others, e.g. the Memories Bundle gives you an item that
        lets you choose a Remembrance card.
      </li>
      <li>
        Recharge: Once a month (or even every 14 days?), you get a one-time bonus on each
        purchase. So you should wait before buying more as it resets. Even with that bonus, these
        offers are usually worse than the other categories.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Battle Pass</h3>
    <p>
      From the start page, the "Pass" is on the right side. It is a monthly battle pass. It
      consists of 3 categories: Homepage, Missions, Remembrances.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Homepage: It has a free track and a premium track. 70 levels in total. Each level
        requires 1000 points. There is a weekly limit of 15k points. Points are earned through
        missions.
      </li>
      <li>
        Depending on your character needs, the premium pass is worth it as it gives you many
        resources and rare items for levelling them up. Just get the standard premium. No need to
        push the +10 levels as you will get to level 70 anyway.
      </li>
      <li>Missions: complete these missions to gain levels for the battle pass.</li>
      <li>Weekly missions: they reset every week, so that they can be repeated.</li>
      <li>
        Period missions: they can be completed only once. Sometimes, an event with character
        selector might be here. Keep an eye on the news, so you do not miss it.
      </li>
      <li>Remembrance: showcase of the current remembrance cards in rotation. Nothing more.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="gacha">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4037-cute.png"
        alt="Lavinia chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Gacha</h2>
    <p>
      You can get strong characters and their remembrances with "Mirage Cubes" and others with
      "Energy Cubes".
    </p>
    <p>
      You can get cubes in various ways: events, market (Featured category), shops (buy them for
      a specific currency, exchange them for 20 dust, exchange them for 160 Luminites),
      missions, achievements, etc.
    </p>
    <p>
      The probability rates and other details are explained on each Gacha page (information icon
      at the top right corner). Dust is earned through playing Gacha.
    </p>
    <p>
      Make sure that you set up the 3x custom selections, so you get characters and remembrances
      that you want.
    </p>
    <p>Recommendations for new players:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Try to get many characters and remembrances so you are able to set up 2 to 3 teams. Do
        not worry about "Awakening" levels for characters yet. More information can be found on
        the wiki.
      </li>
      <li>
        Complete the new player Gacha. It has a better ratio (8x energy cubes for 10x gacha
        rolls) than the other gachas.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="shops">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4008-cute.png"
        alt="Guinevere chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Shops</h2>
    <p>
      From the start page, the "Shop" is on the right side. It consists of many various shops;
      most of them use ingame currency from various activities and events.
    </p>
    <p>
      Here, the best value per cost ratios are recommended (ingame, they are marked by a "value"
      icon or by a small flame icon).
    </p>
    <p>
      The packages in the shops have various reset timers. Some reset once a month, others every
      14 days or even less.
    </p>
    <p>All currency is permanent, as far as the author knows. Nothing gets lost after a season ends.</p>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Dust Shop</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Currency: dust from Gacha rolls. Once a month under "Cube Dust Exchange", get the mirage
        cube, energy cube and the "Original Aether".
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Arena Shop</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Currency: Arena Coins from PvP. Get the rare ones that are marked as "value" or flame
        icon, e.g. Luminites, Cubes, Laser Engraver. Everything else is optional and depends on
        what you need.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Gold Medal Shop</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Currency: Gold Medals, various sources, e.g. from events. Buy Remembrances from the
        current rotation and Laser Engraver for runes creation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Event Exchange Shop</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Currency: event specific. Buy all that are marked as "value" or flame icon, e.g.
        Luminites, Gold Medals, "the Original Aether", Cubes. Other than that, only what you
        currently need for your characters. Note: you must invest a certain currency amount to
        unlock higher rarity options (the concrete numbers are shown on each item).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Starbreaker Shop</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Currency: Annihilation Coins from the Annihilation Battle. Buy all that are marked as
        "value" or flame icon, e.g. Luminites, "the Original Aether", Cubes.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Guild Shop</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Currency: Guild Coins and Guild Conquest Tokens. Buy the rare items like Cubes, Laser
        Engraver, Engraver Card, "the Original Aether", Reshape Dice. Buy the "value" Kappa and
        Iota runes as needed for your characters!
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="events">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4028-cute.png"
        alt="Jorogumo chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Events</h2>
    <p>
      From the start page, the events can be found at the bottom left corner. Usually, each event
      lasts for 14 days.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Featured Events</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Story driven events for event specific currency that can be used in the Event Exchange Shop.</li>
      <li>Get bonus currency for owning specific characters (click on the "Bonus" button for details).</li>
      <li>
        After the featured event is over, the specific Event Exchange Shop stays online for a few
        days more, so that you can exchange your event currency.
      </li>
      <li>
        Each event consists of 13 event story missions with specific rewards (5 free tries each
        day). After they have been completed, you can use the daily free 5 tries for
        auto-collecting the event currency.
      </li>
      <li>
        In addition, there are 5 challenges (Easy, Normal, Hard, Very Hard, Challenge). Completing
        them gives additional rewards (click on the "Rewards" button).
      </li>
      <li>
        Try to do as much as possible from an event because it provides good rewards like e.g.
        "the Original Aether" and Luminites.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Limited Events</h3>
    <p>Gacha, login rewards, special mission rewards. For Gacha, see above.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="missions">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4039-cute.png"
        alt="Nina chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Daily, Weekly and Monthly Missions</h2>
    <p>There are several missions that can be done:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        From the start page, click on "Missions" on the right side. Best way to do the 500 points
        daily: login (100 points), 1 resource raid (200), consume 100 stamina (200; it can be
        combined with one single resource raid to save time). Rewards: Luminite, levelling items,
        account XP, Aether Points.
      </li>
      <li>There are missions in the battle pass (weekly and monthly). See the Battle Pass section for more information.</li>
      <li>There are missions for the guild (weekly). See the Guild section for more information.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="bag">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4038-cute.png"
        alt="Lily chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Items Bag</h2>
    <p>
      From the start page, the bag is located at the centre bottom. It consists of 5 categories:
      Enhancement Materials, Remembrance, Runes, Affinity, Other Items.
    </p>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Enhancement Materials (unlimited storage)</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Contains all items that are needed for levelling up your characters. At the bottom, there
        is a "Synthesize" button. For a small amount of Aether Points, you can synthesize or
        decompose items back and forth as needed to level up your characters. In addition, there
        is a rune craft area. More information on that in the Runes Crafting section.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Remembrance (max 1500 storage)</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Contains all Remembrances. In theory, you can decompose all generic ones to save space.
        However, they barely give any rewards. Also, it might be advisable to lock all valuable
        ones (SSR for sure, maybe even SR) with the "Lock" button. Note that identical
        Remembrances can be used to level up a Remembrance. This increases its power and numbers.
        More information on that in the Characters section.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Runes (max 2000 storage)</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Contains all runes. At the top and at the bottom, there are rune filters. At the bottom,
        there are also 2 buttons for crafting and decomposing runes. More information on that in
        the Runes Crafting section.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Affinity (unlimited storage)</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Contains all training props. In addition, there is a destroy button. However, it provides
        no value.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Other Items (unlimited storage)</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Contains all kinds of items, including special items that you get from shops or the P2W
        market. Note that for some of these items, you need to select them and then click the
        "Use" button to get the reward.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="guild">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4021-cute.png"
        alt="Thor chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Guild</h2>
    <p>From the start page, the guild is located at the centre bottom. Core features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Create and join: players can create their own guild or apply to join existing ones.</li>
      <li>
        Guild level and activity: guilds accumulate experience through members' efforts (e.g.
        completing missions, doing guild conquest and guild battles), raising the guild level.
        Higher levels allow recruiting more members (max 30).
      </li>
      <li>Guild chat: a dedicated guild chat channel lets members discuss tactics and share stories.</li>
      <li>
        Guild shop: actively completing guild missions and guild conquests earns guild currency.
        Actively participating in guild battles provides even more rewards. See the Shops section
        for more information.
      </li>
      <li>Guild log: shows donations and member activity (e.g. joined or left the guild).</li>
      <li>
        Donations: guild members can donate to the guild once per day. The guild leader can use
        them to increase the attack, defense and HP of every member (max lvl 50 each; each level
        provides a 1% bonus). The donations can be farmed at the resource raids. Also, the donor
        gets a small amount of guild currency for the guild shop.
      </li>
      <li>
        Missions (resets weekly): no particular advice here as the 800 points are naturally
        completed by being active.
      </li>
      <li>
        Guild Conquest (reward: guild currency for the guild shop; additional rewards per level
        completed, max 250 levels): this is a guild effort to take down as many bosses as
        possible. Do as much damage as possible to a PvE boss within a time limit. If you have
        strong characters, then a team of 2 supports, 1 damage dealer and 1 tank or healer is the
        best combination for maximum damage. 3 tries daily (requires 3 different teams; a
        character cannot be used twice). Law effects may apply (click on the "Details" button to
        learn about them). Guild rewards are given for up to 250 boss defeats. After that, you
        will still get a small amount of rewards (mostly Aether Points) through the mail system.
        Guild conquest resets weekly.
      </li>
      <li>
        Guild War: occurs every two weeks (12 matches, 1 season). For more information see the
        Guild Wars section.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="guild-wars">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4020-cute.png"
        alt="Odin chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Guild Wars</h2>
    <p>
      In short: take part in it, your leader will assign you to a proper position, use your 3
      attacks on Tuesday and Saturday, get rewards.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Introduction</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Guild battles occur once every two weeks, with a total of 12 matches forming one season.</li>
      <li>
        The group assignment for guild battles is determined based on the previous week's Guild
        Conquest ranking. Once assigned, the same group will be used for 2 consecutive guild
        battles.
      </li>
      <li>
        Guild battles are divided into three main phases: Preparation Phase, Decisive Battle
        Phase, and Settlement Phase.
      </li>
      <li>Preparation Phase: Mondays and Fridays, 05:00:00 to next day 03:59:59 (UTC+8).</li>
      <li>Decisive Battle Phase: Tuesdays and Saturdays, 04:00:00 to next day 23:59:59 (UTC+8).</li>
      <li>Settlement Phase: Thursdays and Mondays, 00:00:00 to 03:59:59 (UTC+8).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Phase Details</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        During the Preparation Phase, guild members can form 2 teams with at least 1 character
        each to participate. Details can be found on the participation page.
      </li>
      <li>
        During the Decisive Battle Phase, only participating guild members can join. Each
        participating member has 3 attack opportunities to assault enemy strongholds. Each attack
        reduces the corresponding HP of the stronghold and gains capture points based on the wins
        and losses of 2 battles. When a stronghold is destroyed, additional capture points are
        gained.
      </li>
      <li>
        During the Settlement Phase, attacks are not allowed. Victory or defeat is determined
        based on the difference in guild capture points. Both winning and losing teams earn guild
        points, with additional guild points awarded based on the number of strongholds
        destroyed. Settlement rewards are distributed via mail to all participating guild
        members.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Stronghold Details</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Stronghold types are divided into: Base, Defense Tower, and Position.</li>
      <li>
        Each type of stronghold has different HP and destruction points. The most important
        stronghold is the Base, which has the highest HP, but when destroyed, the enemy gains
        more additional capture points. Next is the Defense Tower, and finally the Position.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="zguide-note">
      Note: guild battle rewards and settings may be adjusted in different seasons based on the
      current game version. Any changes will be announced in the game announcements. In the
      season settlement rewards, the condition for obtaining guild member rewards is
      participating in at least one guild war during the season.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="characters">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4057-cute.png"
        alt="Medusa chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Characters</h2>
    <p>
      From the start page, the characters screen can be found at the bottom right corner. For
      each character, it consists of 9 important categories and buttons:
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Details</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        4 important buttons here on the right side: Attributes, Skills, Level Up/Ascend and
        Bonding.
      </li>
      <li>Note also the information button near the class. It explains the class function.</li>
      <li>There is also a details button with more statistics.</li>
      <li>
        Each character has 5 skills: a normal attack (NA; it has a cooldown), a combo (only
        active if the requirement is met), a skill (used automatically; it has a cooldown), a
        passive (permanently active) and an ultimate (manual or auto activation possible; it has
        energy cost and a cooldown).
      </li>
      <li>
        Characters can be levelled up and ascended to max level 80. Every 10 levels, specific
        ascend items are needed to progress further.
      </li>
      <li>
        Bonding increases the stats of a character and unlocks new art and clips. It requires
        class specific training props. You can use 30 of them daily for free. Natural
        regeneration: 1 attempt per 30 minutes. If you cannot wait, you will need additional
        "bonding attempts" items.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Remembrances</h3>
    <p>
      Set and enhance a remembrance the same way a character is levelled up. It increases its
      stats. In addition, it can be awakened 5 times for even more stats with the same
      remembrance cards.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Talents</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Talents and skills can be increased here.</li>
      <li>
        The most critical resource and bottleneck here is "the Original Aether". Everything else
        can be raided and synthesized.
      </li>
      <li>
        It is very expensive to level up skills past level 7. Consider investing your resources
        in a different character first.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Runes</h3>
    <p>Set and level up runes as described in the Runes Crafting section.</p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Awaken</h3>
    <p>
      When you get a second copy of the girl, it can be invested here to increase her abilities.
      Check out the wiki for recommendations on which awakening levels are worth it.
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Info</h3>
    <p>Dialog and story content.</p>

    <p>
      From the start page, please also note the "Codex" on the right side. It lists all girls and
      remembrances, even the ones that you do not own yet. In addition, all unlocked main story
      and event story parts can be revisited here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="runes">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4053-cute.png"
        alt="Nephthys chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Runes Crafting</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are 6 runes: I, II, III, IV, V, VI.</li>
      <li>Craft the runes as recommended for the character builds in the wiki.</li>
      <li>Use the laser engraver to set the main stat of runes IV, V and VI.</li>
      <li>Optional: use an engraver card to set one secondary stat.</li>
      <li>
        Level up the rune to level 10. Levels 11 to 15 are quite expensive (see the wiki graph
        for more details).
      </li>
      <li>
        More information about rune crafting including screenshots can be found on the wiki:
        the <a href="/guides/zone-nova/runes/">runes overview</a>, the
        <a href="/guides/zone-nova/crafting/">crafting guide</a> and the
        <a href="/guides/zone-nova/crafting-items/">crafting items list</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      When crafting, flat stats are usually worse than % stats. Aim for % stats mainly (except
      for HP, where flat and % are both worth it).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="teams">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4058-cute.png"
        alt="Brynhild chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Team Compositions</h2>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Classes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Tank: Defensive Vanguard</li>
      <li>Warrior (DPS): Balanced Fighter</li>
      <li>Attacker (DPS): Single-Target Striker</li>
      <li>Destroyer (DPS): AoE Striker</li>
      <li>Supporter: Buff Support</li>
      <li>Disruptor: Disruption Support</li>
      <li>Healer: Recovery Support</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Compositions</h3>
    <p>
      The usual setup is Tank (position 1), DPS as in Warrior/Attacker/Destroyer (position 2),
      Support/Disruptor (position 3), Healer (position 4).
    </p>
    <p>
      Some characters are so strong that only 1 tank or healer is required. In that case, go for
      this setup for maximum damage: OP char (position 1), Support/Disruptor (position 2),
      Support/Disruptor (position 3), Healer (position 4; alternative: Tank on position 1, OP char
      on position 2).
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">Combos</h3>
    <p>
      Most of the time, you want to create a team where all 4 combos are active! However, in some
      situations, it is not possible for certain characters that are still worth using because
      they are very strong (e.g. Medusa).
    </p>

    <h3 class="zguide-subtitle">PvP</h3>
    <p>For PvP setups, please check the replays in the tournament history records (Hall of Fame).</p>
    <p>
      Further recommendations can be found in the wiki
      <a href="/guides/zone-nova/tier-list/">tier list</a> and the
      <a href="/guides/zone-nova/character-builds/">character builds</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="zguide-section" id="attributes">
      <img
        class="zguide-corner-chibi"
        src="https://k2b1c5ab57ed98e51.gachawiki.info/zone-nova/avatars/4054-cute.png"
        alt="Bedivere chibi avatar"
        width=72
        height=72
        loading="lazy"
      />
    <h2 class="zguide-title">Glossary (Attributes and Skills)</h2>
    <p>General definitions for all entries in this list:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Durations are defined in seconds.</li>
      <li>
        Increases, decreases and reductions are always defined in percentages (unless specified
        differently in the list below).
      </li>
      <li>
        In this list, for efficiency reasons, the term "ally" includes self. This might not be
        true for all ingame skills. Please check ingame.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Make sure to read the wiki on this. Its data is directly from the game files:
      <a href="/guides/zone-nova/damage-mechanics/">damage mechanics</a>,
      <a href="/guides/zone-nova/damage-mechanics/modifier-system/">combat modifiers</a> and
      <a href="/guides/zone-nova/damage-mechanics/core-formulas/">damage formulas</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Armor Shatter</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Reduce enemy defense by 3% for the specified duration.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Attack</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Attack Power.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Attack Attributes</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Blaze, Chaos, Frost, Holy, Storm Damage. Multiplier for the specific element skill.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Attack Increase</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Increases ally attack attribute.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Attack Reduction</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Decreases enemy attack attribute.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Attack Speed</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Attacks per second (note: this is not the same as cooldown, see the Athena passive
        description). Applies to normal attack only!
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Attack Speed Increase</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Increases ally attack speed (note: this is not the same as cooldown, see the Athena
        passive description).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Base Attack</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Baseline of the normal attack. See the
        <a href="/guides/zone-nova/damage-mechanics/">wiki</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Base Attack Speed</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Raises the baseline of the normal attack speed. See the
        <a href="/guides/zone-nova/damage-mechanics/">wiki</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Base Skill Cooldown</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
        Improves the baseline of the normal attack cooldown. See the
        <a href="/guides/zone-nova/damage-mechanics/">wiki</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Block</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Reduce damage taken by 30%. Damage over time ignores block.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Block Rate</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Trigger block based on a percentage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Buff Duration</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">Duration of a buff.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zguide-def">
      <div class="zguide-def-term">Channel</div>
      <p class="zguide-def-desc">
